  "saveFile": "minimal_colony.rws",
  "description": "Clear weather left alone for about nine in-game hours, to show that \u00a725's cloud population is decoupled from the instantaneous cover: a sheet keeps the cover it entered under until it has drifted off the map (CloudSheetLayout.EntryTickFor). MEASURED SERIES, 16 frames 1,500 ticks apart -- cover wandered 0.211 -> 0.271 -> 0.000, crossing a sheet threshold five times; the drawn mass changed three times, each at a wrap. The last two frames are the ones worth looking at: cover is exactly 0.0000 and the sky still has cloud in it, because two sheets are finishing their crossings. Before the latch, cover reaching zero emptied the sky in one tick, wherever the clouds happened to be. ONLY THE FIRST FRAME IS PINNED: every later one sits after a FastForward, which overshoots its target by a frame-rate-dependent margin, so those readings are not reproducible between runs. They are recorded in the report to be read, not asserted on."
}